#3600
The Foyer of the Lyceum~
   A high, gilded foyer, its plaster ceiling painted with masks and
garlands that the damp has started to peel.  Brass lamps burn in their
sconces and a worn red carpet runs from the street doors in the north to a
pair of padded doors in the south, which open into the auditorium.  Beside
them stands the box office, a little booth of carved wood with a brass
grille, and a playbill is pasted to the wall beneath a lamp.
~
