#3601
The Auditorium of the Lyceum~
   Rows of red plush seats, worn bald on the arms, slope down toward a
wide wooden stage framed by a gilded proscenium arch.  Footlights in brass
cups line the front of the stage, and a heavy velvet curtain the colour of
old wine hangs above it.  The air smells of greasepaint, candle smoke and
oranges.  A small door at stage left, half hidden by the curtain, leads
west into the wings, and the padded doors to the foyer are at the back of
the hall.
~
