#3602
The Wings~
   Behind the proscenium the theatre is all ropes and shadows.  Lines run
up from cleats on the wall into the darkness of the fly loft, where the
painted backdrops hang folded like the wings of great bats.  Flats of
painted scenery lean against the brickwork: a castle wall, a moonlit
forest, a ship's rail.  The small door to the stage is east; a passage
runs south to the dressing rooms, and the prop room is west.
~
