#3603
The Dressing Rooms~
   A long, low room lined with mirrors, each framed by a ring of candle
stubs.  Costumes hang from every hook and rafter: crowns of gilt paper,
cloaks of dyed sacking, a dragon's head with one eye missing.  The tables
are crowded with pots of greasepaint, powder puffs and bitten apples, and
a battered sofa sags beneath a pile of wigs.  The wings are back north.
~
