#3606
A Damp Brick Tunnel~
   An old brick tunnel, arched and slick with damp, older by far than the
theatre above it.  Water drips from the roots that have pushed through the
mortar, and the floor is a paste of mud and droppings.  The gnawed hole
into the cellar is west; the tunnel runs on east, and a low opening leads
south.
~
