#3611
The Gnawed Passage~
   Every inch of this passage has been gnawed: the bricks are pitted, the
old beams are shredded to splinters, and bones crunch underfoot - bird
bones, cat bones, and some that are rather bigger.  A rank, warm smell
comes from the east.  A narrower way leads west, and the cistern is north.
~
